# Pidlwick II, the clockwork jester of the high tower (docs/voice/pidlwick_ii.md). The marionette card's ally.
# He never speaks aloud: his lines are mime in parentheses and the words he chalks on a little slate, in capitals.
# start: on the grand landing (approach). cards: the ally scene (join pidlwick_ii). key_back: the other way he joins.
# His secret (he pushed the first Pidlwick down the stair) comes out by Insight, the portrait by the well, or Escher.

~ start
if guest:pidlwick_ii
-> companion
endif
if not flag.pidlwick_met
-> first
endif
if flag.pidlwick_refused
Narrator [away]: Pidlwick II sits on the top step with his back to you. When you come close he shuffles along to make room, without turning round.
else
Narrator: Pidlwick II bounces up off the step, bells jingling, and bows so low that his cap brushes the stone.
endif
-> menu

~ first
set pidlwick_met
Narrator: Something small comes down the stair toward you, one careful step at a time: a jester the height of a child, in faded motley and a cap of bells, with a painted porcelain face. Gears tick inside it.
Narrator: It stops two steps above you, makes a deep and complicated bow, and holds up a little slate. Chalked on it, in crooked capitals:
Pidlwick II: HELLO. I AM PIDLWICK. THE SECOND.
interject class:wizard: Clockwork, and very old. Somebody loved making this.
Pidlwick II: (He wipes the slate with his sleeve and writes again, quickly.) PLAY?
-> menu

~ menu
* [if tarokka.ally.npc == pidlwick_ii and not flag.pidlwick_refused] Madam Eva's cards showed us a clockwork jester. -> cards
* [if flag.pidlwick_key_found and not flag.pidlwick_wound] We found your key. -> key_back
* Who made you? -> maker
* [if not flag.pidlwick_wary and not flag.pidlwick_truth_known] Was there another Pidlwick? A first one? -> first_one
* [if not flag.pidlwick_truth_known and (flag.jester_portrait_seen or flag.escher_told_jester)] We know what happened to the first Pidlwick. -> confront
* [if not flag.pidlwick_played] Play a game with him. -> play
* [if not quest.the_jesters_key] You're ticking slowly. Are you all right? -> winding
* You know this castle. Show us its secrets. -> secrets
* Goodbye, Pidlwick. -> bye

~ maker
Pidlwick II: A TOYMAKER. LONG AGO. FOR THE CHILDREN OF THE HOUSE.
Narrator: He mimes a ring of small people laughing, and himself in the middle, juggling. Then the ring fades away and he goes on juggling alone.
if flag.blinsky_met
interject tag:cheerful: There's a toymaker in Vallaki with a cap just like yours. He'd love you. He'd take you apart to see how you work, but he'd love you.
Pidlwick II: (He clutches his cap with both hands and backs up a step.) NO.
endif
-> menu

~ first_one
Narrator: The ticking inside him stops. Then it starts again, a little faster.
Pidlwick II: HE FELL. STAIRS. LONG AGO.
* [Insight DC 14] That isn't the whole story, is it? -> truth_seen | truth_missed
* Poor thing. -> menu

~ truth_seen
Narrator: He holds your eye for a long moment, his painted face smiling the smile it was painted with. Then he wipes the slate very slowly and writes, small:
-> truth

~ truth_missed
set pidlwick_wary
Narrator: He tucks the slate behind his back and turns a cartwheel down three steps, as if nobody had asked anything. When he comes up again he won't look toward the well.
-> menu

~ confront
Narrator: You tell him what you know. He listens with his head on one side and his bells quite still. Then he writes, small:
-> truth

~ truth
set pidlwick_truth_known
Pidlwick II: THEY LOVED HIM. NOT ME. SO I HELPED HIM DOWN.
Pidlwick II: SORRY. VERY SORRY. FOR A VERY LONG TIME.
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: Sorry for a very long time. That is a long penance, little one. Be at peace.
interject tag:blunt: He pushed a man down a tower because he was jealous. Let's not forget it.
-> menu

~ play
set pidlwick_played
time +10
Narrator: Three wooden balls appear from nowhere and he tosses you one. For a few minutes, on a stair in a vampire's house, you play catch with a clockwork jester, and he is very good at it.
interject name:wren_featherfoot: He palmed one. Saw it. Lovely wrist on him. I'd have been quicker, but lovely.
Pidlwick II: (A deep bow, then the slate.) AGAIN? LATER?
approve wren_featherfoot +2: You played catch with a clockwork jester on a vampire's stair
-> menu

~ winding
Narrator [away]: He sags a little, as if the question let the air out of him, and turns round to show you a keyhole in his back. It is empty.
Pidlwick II: KEY. THE BIRDS TOOK IT. UP UNDER THE ROOF.
Pidlwick II: I WIND MYSELF WITH A NAIL. IT IS NOT THE SAME.
quest the_jesters_key asked
* We'll look for it. -> menu
* Can't you fetch it yourself? -> winding_why

~ winding_why
Pidlwick II: THE BIRDS DO NOT LIKE ME. I TAKE THEIR SHINY THINGS. THEY TAKE MINE.
-> menu

~ secrets
Pidlwick II: (He points up the stair, bells jingling.) TOP: THE GLASS HEART. HE GOES THERE WHEN HE IS HURT.
if not flag.heart_of_sorrow_known
set heart_of_sorrow_known
endif
if not quest.the_heart_of_sorrow
quest the_heart_of_sorrow heard
endif
Pidlwick II: (He points across, toward the tower rooms.) SAD MAN IN THE LOCKED ROOM. STAIR BEHIND HIS CUPBOARD. UP TO THE BIRDS.
set spires_back_stair_told
Pidlwick II: (Last of all he points at the well, and then quickly away from it.) DO NOT LEAN.
-> start

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- The ally (Madam Eva's marionette card)

~ cards
Narrator: He drops the slate. He picks it up, writes, rubs it out, and writes again.
Pidlwick II: ME? THE CARDS SAID ME?
Pidlwick II: NOBODY EVER PICKS ME.
-> cards_choice

~ cards_choice
* Come with us, Pidlwick. -> join
* [if flag.pidlwick_truth_known and not flag.pidlwick_promised] We know what you did to the first Pidlwick. Why should we trust you? -> cards_truth
* We won't take you. -> refuse
* Not yet. -> menu

~ cards_truth
set pidlwick_promised
Pidlwick II: (He writes for a long time, and holds the slate up with both hands.) I WILL NOT PUSH. I WILL WALK BEHIND. ALWAYS BEHIND. PROMISE.
-> cards_choice

~ join
Narrator: He turns three cartwheels down the landing, bells going like a sleigh, and stops in front of you at attention.
join pidlwick_ii
if tarokka.ally.npc == pidlwick_ii
quest find_the_ally found
endif
attitude pidlwick_ii friendly
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: Welcome aboard, little fellow! You walk beside me. Nobody walks behind anybody on a stair. New rule.
Pidlwick II: (He salutes with the wrong hand.) YES SIR.
approve godrick_pendlebrook +1 wren_featherfoot +1: You let Pidlwick come along
-> END

~ refuse
set pidlwick_refused
if tarokka.ally.npc == pidlwick_ii
quest find_the_ally lost
endif
Narrator: He nods, very politely, and sits down on the top step with the slate in his lap. He doesn't write anything else.
-> END

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- His key (the other way he joins)

~ key_back
set pidlwick_wound
quest the_jesters_key returned
Narrator [away]: You hold out the brass key. He goes perfectly still, then turns his back to you and waits.
Narrator: It takes a long time to wind him: forty turns, fifty. With every turn his ticking grows steadier.
Pidlwick II: (He spins on one toe.) THANK YOU. THANK YOU. THANK YOU.
Pidlwick II: A PRESENT. I KEPT IT IN MY HAT FOR A HUNDRED YEARS. (He holds out a fly carved of black wood.) IT GROWS. DON'T TELL ANYONE.
give figurine_of_wondrous_power_ebony_fly
if guest:pidlwick_ii
-> companion
endif
if not flag.pidlwick_refused
Pidlwick II: CAN I COME WITH YOU? I KNOW ALL THE STAIRS.
endif
* [if not flag.pidlwick_refused] Come with us, Pidlwick. -> join
* [if not flag.pidlwick_refused] Better stay here, where it's safe. -> stay
* [if flag.pidlwick_refused] Goodbye, Pidlwick. -> bye

~ stay
Pidlwick II: (He nods. He is used to it.) SAFE. YES.
-> menu

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Travelling with the party

~ companion
Pidlwick II: (He tugs your sleeve and holds up the slate.) WHERE NOW?
* [if flag.pidlwick_key_found and not flag.pidlwick_wound] We found your key. -> key_back
* Show us the castle's secrets. -> secrets
* How are you holding up? -> companion_how
* Wait for us on the stair. -> companion_wait
* Nothing. Let's go. -> END

~ companion_how
if flag.heart_of_sorrow_shattered
Pidlwick II: THE HEART IS QUIET. THE HOUSE IS LISTENING FOR IT. (He shivers, bells and all.)
elif flag.pidlwick_wound
Pidlwick II: WOUND UP. TICKING. HAPPY.
else
Pidlwick II: TICKING. MOSTLY. (He winds himself a little with a bent nail.)
endif
-> companion

~ companion_wait
leave pidlwick_ii
Pidlwick II: (He trots off toward the high tower.) ON THE STAIR. DO NOT FORGET ME.
-> END

~ bye
Narrator: He waves with his whole arm until you are out of sight.
-> END
